    "problem": "Creating accurate, high-resolution global maps of ocean pH is challenging because historical measurements are sparse and unreliable, and Earth System Models alone do not always reflect the true ocean state, often being initialized with spatially limited observational data.",
    "method": "The authors create a high-resolution global surface ocean pH climatology by combining a recent, dense observational CO2 data product with long-term temporal trends from a robust Earth System Model to reconstruct past and project future conditions from 1750 to 2100.",
